    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12538796/comment/13188440",
          "id": "13188440",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "body": "Forgot to mention that Doron actually discovered the bug, I just had the time to provide the fix :).",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "created": "2012-01-18T13:37:46.548+0000",
          "updated": "2012-01-18T13:37:46.548+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12538796/comment/13188444",
          "id": "13188444",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "body": "Patch fixes the bug by moving to track reference count by DTR. Also, added a test which covers that bug.\n\nOn the go, fixed close() to synchronize on this if the instance is not already closed. Otherwise, two threads that call close() concurrently might fail (one of them) in decRef().\n\nI think it's ready to commit, will wait until tomorrow for review.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "created": "2012-01-18T13:46:11.839+0000",
          "updated": "2012-01-18T13:46:11.839+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12538796/comment/13188975",
          "id": "13188975",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=doronc",
            "name": "doronc",
            "key": "doronc",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738"
            },
            "displayName": "Doron Cohen",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Gaza"
          },
          "body": "Patch looks good, builds and passes for me, thanks for fixing this Shai.\n\nFew comments:\n* CHANGES: rephrase the e.g. part like this: (e.g. if application called incRef/decRef).\n* New test:\n** LTC.newDirectory() instead of new RAMDirectory().\n** text messages in the asserts.\n* DTR: \n** Would it be simpler to make close() synchronized (just like IR.close())\n** Would it - again - be simpler to keep maintaining the ref-counts in the internal IR and just, in refresh, decRef as needed in the old one and incRef accordingly in the new one? This way we continue to delegate that logic to IR, and do not duplicate it.\n** Current patch removes the ensureOpen() check from getRefCount(). I think this is correct - in fact I needed that when debugging this. Perhaps should document about it in CHANGES entry.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=doronc",
            "name": "doronc",
            "key": "doronc",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738"
            },
            "displayName": "Doron Cohen",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Gaza"
          },
          "created": "2012-01-19T07:37:52.908+0000",
          "updated": "2012-01-19T07:37:52.908+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12538796/comment/13188990",
          "id": "13188990",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
